# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify-style redirect rules.
#
# /services/ is not a second Services hub — proposal.md §24 (P0) explicitly
# requires root "/" to be the ONE master Services landing page and forbids
# building a competing "/services/" hub. This is a plain alias, not new
# content: it just closes the 404 an old link, a direct URL guess, or a
# search engine's own convention-guessing might hit, since "Services" is the
# first primary nav label. See NOTES.md → "Architectural decisions made
# without further sign-off" and docs/tasks/TASK-009 for the reasoning.
/services/      /       301
/ru/services/   /ru/    301
/th/services/   /th/    301
/he/services/   /he/    301
